<title>GREECE: Greek inflation below 5.5 pct in May, PM Simitis.</title>
<headline>Greek inflation below 5.5 pct in May, PM Simitis.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek Prime Minister Costas Simitis said on Monday that inflation would drop below 5.5 percent in May from 5.9 percent in April.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect inflation to drop below 5.5 percent in May,&quot; Simitis told parliament during a debate on the economy.</p>
<p>Simitis said that despite the positive trend Greek inflation was still high compared to inflation rates in the other European Union countries.</p>
<p>--Costas Paris, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
